    "extraction_notes": [
      "Transfer, output, and capacitance curve families needed for an F2 attempt are present on p. 3 and were digitized with SI units.",
      "The transfer curve uses the TJ = 25 degC trace. The figure axis is labeled in mA and the extracted y values are converted to A.",
      "The output curves use the VGS = 4 V, 5 V, and 10 V traces at TJ = 25 degC. The figure y axis is labeled in A and the extracted values are retained in A.",
      "The capacitance curves use the VGS = 0 V traces. The p. 2 capacitance table specifies f = 1 MHz and VDS = 25 V; the p. 3 figure does not repeat the frequency annotation.",
      "The p. 3 Ciss trace reads near 20 pF at VDS = 25 V, while the p. 2 table lists 30 pF at VDS = 25 V. Both published values are retained: the table value is in specs.ciss and the curve reading is in curves.",
      "No typical VGS(th) value appears in the Electrical Characteristics table. The 2 V typical value is taken from the p. 1 Features summary, while the p. 2 threshold test condition is retained.",
      "The datasheet publishes RDS(on) maximum limits at VGS = 10 V and 4.5 V, both at TJ = 25 degC, with no typical RDS(on) table values.",
      "The datasheet publishes RthJA but no RthJC, and publishes VSD but no body-diode trr. These omissions limit thermal and reverse-recovery fitting.",
      "Breakdown voltage is specified at ID = 10 uA, not at 250 uA."
    ],
    "omission_reason": "F2 curve extraction is supported, but RthJC and body-diode trr are not published, the typical threshold value is only in the feature summary, and the p. 2 Ciss table conflicts with the p. 3 Ciss curve. Digitized curve points are approximate readings from the supplied figures."
